Magic mapping REALLY helped speed up Gehennom. Without it I'd probably
spend just as much time as I did in the main dungeon, and the game
would be twice as long. With magic mapping it was just a business-like
matter of cast magic map, dig through to down stairs, cast magic map,
kill major demon, dig through to down stairs, cast magic map, note
Vlad's tower, etc.. That did mean that I didn't explore the levels
fully, though. With the exception of the Valley, I probably only
covered 10%-15% of what's there. So I probably missed out a lot of
valuable gems and other equipment that were generated.

My score wasn't that great compared to my previous Samurai ascension.
I suspect this had a lot to do with the fact I left a lot of valuable
loot in the stash (somehow I got this paranoid feeling that I don't
want to risk carrying too much into the planes, and should travel as
light as possible). Probably also because many of my gems got
destroyed in the BoH accident, which included all the Mine bottom
gems. Why I had to carry them around compulsively is beyond me, in
retrospect.


